---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Labs"
seoTitle: "Labs: free step-by-step tools for Operations Research and Business Statistics"
permalink: /tools/
description: "Two free labs for B.B.A. students. OR Lab for Operations Research, and Stats Lab for Business Mathematics and Statistics. Enter a problem from your textbook and each tool works it out step by step."
keywords: ["operations research calculator", "business statistics calculator", "LPP solver", "transportation problem", "matrix calculator", "correlation", "regression"]
pageCss: /assets/or-lab/or-lab.css
---
{% set labs = [
  { d: orlab, href: "/tools/or/", course: "operations-research", icon: "network" },
  { d: statlab, href: "/tools/stats/", course: "business-mathematics-statistics", icon: "bars" }
] %}
<div class="wrap page">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">For students</p>
    <h1>Labs</h1>
    <p class="lead">Free, interactive tools for two B.B.A. papers. Enter a problem from your textbook or class, and each tool works it out step by step, the way you would by hand, so you can check your own working.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="lab-units">
    {% for lab in labs %}
    <section class="lab-unit" aria-labelledby="lab-{{ loop.index }}">
      <div class="lab-hub-head">
        {% if lab.icon == "network" %}
        <svg class="lab-hub-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="5" cy="6" r="2.5"/><circle cx="19" cy="6" r="2.5"/><circle cx="12" cy="18" r="2.5"/><path d="M7.5 6h9M6.3 8.3l4.4 7.5M17.7 8.3l-4.4 7.5"/></svg>
        {% else %}
        <svg class="lab-hub-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 20.5h18"/><rect x="4.5" y="12" width="3.5" height="8.5" rx=".5"/><rect x="10.25" y="5" width="3.5" height="15.5" rx=".5"/><rect x="16" y="9" width="3.5" height="11.5" rx=".5"/></svg>
        {% endif %}
        <h2 id="lab-{{ loop.index }}"><a href="{{ lab.href }}">{{ lab.d.name }}</a></h2>
        <p>{{ lab.d.paper }}</p>
        <p class="lab-hub-count">{{ lab.d.tools | dictsort | length }} tools</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="tool-list">
          {% for u in lab.d.units %}{% for slug in u.tools %}
          <li><a href="/tools/{{ slug }}/"><span class="tool-unit">Unit {{ u.no }}</span><span class="tool-name">{{ lab.d.tools[slug].title }}</span></a></li>
          {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p class="tools-more"><a href="{{ lab.href }}">{{ lab.d.name }}: what each tool does</a></p>
        {% set notes = collections.resources | byCourse(lab.course) %}
        {% if notes.length %}<p class="lab-hub-notes">Study notes for the paper: {% for n in notes %}<a href="{{ n.url }}">{{ n.data.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </section>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <section class="lab-unit" aria-labelledby="about-lab">
    <h2 class="lab-unit-head" id="about-lab"><span class="unit-no">How to use them</span></h2>
    <div class="lab-about">
      <p>Work the problem by hand first, then enter it here to check each step: the tools show the tables and the arithmetic in the order you would write them in an exam, not just the final answer.</p>
      <p>Everything is worked out in your browser, so nothing you type is sent anywhere. “Copy link to this problem” gives a link that opens the same problem, ready to share with a class.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
